# Vitreo (2026-09-28, video pass), x64 = x86: 101 differing lines, all attributed:
#   [caps YUY2] fs2 0x00010480 -> 0x480: FORMAT_SUPPORT2_DISPLAYABLE (displayable surfaces /
#     SHARED_DISPLAYABLE) is not implemented; NV12's (d3d11_nv12_probe) likewise.
#   "size 16386x2" (every format): Metal textures stop at 16384 (the documented 2D limit);
#     WARP creates past it.
#   [views YUY2] R8G8_B8G8_UNORM SRV and its ldb8g8 lines: refused, UNIMPLEMENTED -- no Metal
#     texel format views the half-width storage as a full-width RGB-rebuilding format.
#   [layout Y210] / [layout Y216] dynld/ldf/ldu dims and texels: WARP reports the
#     R16G16B16A16 view at the resource's full width and reads texels past W/2 from the next
#     row (x in [W/2, W) of row y = row y+1's pairs, the last row's zeros); Learn maps one view
#     texel to a pixel pair (Y0, U, Y1, V), which is what this runtime gives (W/2 wide).
#   [layout Y416] "ldf linear": one ULP in a bilinear sample (filtering is inexact, D3D11.3 7.18).
